WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
Hi, I'm Eric Voss

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.280
And Captain Marvel ain't just an origin story
 for Captain Marvel,

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.240
the newest hero to join the Avengers,

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.980
it's also an origin story for Nick Fury and Phil Coulson!

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.180
Uncannily deep faked into children,

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.040
because this movie ties into the MCU
in so many interesting ways.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.200
Subtle nods to the Guardians of the Galaxy, Avengers, Winter Soldier, even the Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.080
Maybe even saying where the MCU could go beyond Endgame!

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.600
So let's re-watch this movie scene-by-scene

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.000
break it all down for all the Easter eggs and
film-making details that you might've missed

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.960
Spoiler warning, in case you haven't
seen Captain Marvel yet

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.400
I will ruin your life.
Let's get started.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.400
OK.  Before this movie even begins,
there's a big Marvel shout-out

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.000
In the form of a tribute to the late, great Stan Lee

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.380
With this being the first Marvel Studios film release
since his passing.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.200
The studio's title sequence
has replaced the various Avengers

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.960
with Stan from his many cameos.
Including:

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.820
the FedEX driver in Civil War,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.220
*Stan Lee impression*
Package for Tony Stank

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.180
as Hugh Hefner in the first Iron Man,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.800
the Sakaar barber in Ragnarok,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.220
the World War II general in the first Captain America,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.580
and the drunk vet. in Age of Ultron.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.420
Also, the guy on the bus in Doctor Strange.
Tons of others.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.280
It's a touching memorial, but I just love how this reminds us

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.700
how Stan is an actual physical person!

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.000
Physically many people

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.780
throughout this whole movie universe

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:12.200
And despite his departure from our world, his presence still lives on in the cinematic world

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.780
The opening frame show us the cryptic dream of
our hero, Carol Danvers (Brie Larsen),

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.000
as she tries to piece together her past

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.280
A mysterious accident that led to gaining super-natural abilities

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.180
It's fitting that this movie using this whole
'fractured memory' device,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.300
because in the comics Captain Marvel's whole history is ridiculously complicated.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.580
Originally, the character was male, a Kree warrior known as Mar-Vell.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.300
I know, it's goofy,
but there already was a Captain Marvel in comics;

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.820
the DC hero, who the young Billy Batson turns into
when he says "SHAZAM!"

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.000
Over time Marvel was able to stick to the name
'Captain Marvel' for their hero

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.360
and DC just started calling their guy 'Shazam'

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.600
And it's not at all confusing that
movies for Captain Marvel

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.600
and Shazam are released with a month of each other

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.440
Anyway Captain Marvel had a female counterpart named Ms. Marvel over the years.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.380
With an interesting wardrobe

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.560
And a few decades later,
Captain Marvel was relaunched

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.440
as a United States Air Force pilot, Carol Danvers

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.980
Who directly took on the Kree powers
and the mantle of 'Captain Marvel'

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.340
Which had been a very popular series by comic writer Kelly Sue DeConnick

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.620
Here Annet Bening plays the Kree scientist
named Mar-Vell,

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.060
who brings Danvers into the fold;
we'll get to her backstory later

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.360
Danvers, or as she's known here 'Vers'

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.580
from the second half of her last-name
on her severed dog-tag,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.960
Wakes up on the Kree planet of Hala.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.140
The Kree are a race of genetically superior warriors

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.900
and they're locked in a perennial war with the Skrull,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.000
a race of shapeshifters

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.220
The Kree have shown up in Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.,
as well as the Guardians of the Galaxy movies

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.580
like Ronan the Accuser and Korath are Kree
who show up in both films.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.600
In Captain marvel they're still part of the Kree military

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.620
Later on, in Guardians, they'll be extremists
disavowed by the Kree leadership.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:45.180
But still, the Kree race
has never been cast in a positive light.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.000
"He is slaughtering children.  Families."

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.340
"*That* is your business."

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.040
"Now, I have other matters to attend to."

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:55.880
"Prick."

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.500
Actually, early drafts of the first Guardians of the Galaxy

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.000
and of this movie were written by the same screenwriter, Nicole Perlman.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.800
So they do share a sort of DNA

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.280
For example, just as they do in the Guardians movies,

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.980
every time a new planet or location is introduced,

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.640
notice how navigation co-ordinates appear beneath the name of the place.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.200
Vers spars with her mentor, Jude Laws' character

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.420
His name wasn't really spoken aloud much,
but it is Yon-Rogg

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.940
And that's because Yon-Rogg is Captain Marvel's long-time Kree nemesis in the comics

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.580
and we later find out that this guy is a bad guy

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.400
As they spar Vers is prevented from powering up fully by this inhibitor ship in her neck

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.020
This is similar to the inhibitor that was used on Quake
in Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.860
A show where a lot of the gadgetry could have been base don Kree technology.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.780
Vers meets with the Kree Supreme Intelligence;

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.960
it's an A.I. authority that, in the comics,
takes the form of a Zordon-y disembodied face

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:46.880
But here, it takes on a different form to each Kree; whomever they most admire.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.620
For Vers it's Annet Bening (Mar-Vell), as a way for her subconscious try to help her unlock the truth of her past

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.740
But this could also be a manipulation by
the Supreme Intelligence

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:59.980
Perhaps as a way to further confuse Vers about Annet Bening showing up in her dreams

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.040
Like if you have sex dreams about your teacher

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.460
You would probably assume it's a weird coincidence

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.180
of someone you see all the time slipping
into your subconscious.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.380
And not that your teacher really was someone
you slept with in the past that you just blocked out.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.540
By the way, nice.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.860
*South Park "Nice" montage*

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.520
In the comics, the Supreme Intelligence is
cruelly manipulative, just like this

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.860
And actually turns out to have orchestrated
a self-genocide on the Kree race

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.200
To force the survivors to evolve
and break out of their genetic stagnation

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.160
Not very nice.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.000
The Supreme Intelligence assigns Vers to the Star Force

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.680
Which is kind of like SEAL Team Six of the Kree military

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.400
They're led by Yon-Rogg.  They also include:

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.660
Korath (Djimon Hounsou)

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.020
Minn-Erva, Gemma Chan's character, she's a Kree geneticist in the comics

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.440
Att-Lass, Captain Atlus from the comics
played by Algenis Perez Soto

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.680
And Bron-Char! Played by Rune Temte

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.400
In the comics, Bron-Char wasn't really
a member of the Star force,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.580
but his claim to fame was he was a Kree soldier who broke one of Captain America's shields

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.000
Also notice how the production designers of this movie use the same sets and backdrops of Hala

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.620
that we saw behind the Kree delegate in 
Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.580
Great consistency.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.280
And when the Star Force ships depart Hala,
they pass through these hexagonal wormholes

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:07.000
This is also a production design detail from the Guardians movies

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.540
In Volume 2, Rocket, Groot, Yondu and Kraglin

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.960
used the same intergalactic travel technology

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.800
The mission is the extraction of a spy
from the planet Torfa

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:18.900
It's a location also from the comics.
Actually a Skrull refugee planet

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:23.040
Hinting that these Skrull that they find are
actually refugees, not hostile invaders.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.380
Also, Torfa is known for a toxic atmosphere caused by vibranium.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:31.180
Suggesting that this planet could have been formed by the same astronomical event

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.120
that caused that vibranium meteorite
that struck Wakanda on Earth.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.000
During this mission we see how Vers' Kree suit
projects a mask over her face.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.820
This looks a lot like the same technology
that Peter Quill uses for his mask.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.940
And that whole spacesuit that they use in Volume 2.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.820
They all got it from the Kree.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.780
This mission of course ends up being a trap, for the Skrull to capture Vers and scrub her memories

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.000
The Skrull are led by Talos,
not the pronunciation I thought it was gonna be,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.320
played by Ben Mendelsohn.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.000
Now, in the comics he's known as Talos the Untamed

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.820
He's got a fierce reputation, a Skrull warrior

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.560
But that changes when he gets captured by the Kree

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.500
and refuses to commit their whole ritualistic suicide where they shift into the face of their captor

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.800
And this all earns him the name 'Talos the Tamed'

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:08.520
Burn.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:11.640
Similarly in this movie,
Talos does work with some of the Kree

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.600
But really the Skrull, as we see them in this movie,

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.620
have been changed drastically
from what we know from comics.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.200
Vers relives her memories as Carol Danvers,
U.S. Air Force pilot

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.380
Alongside her friend maria Rambeau (Lashana Lynch)

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.840
Notice how Maria's call sign is "Photon"

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.340
That's a nod to her daughter, Monica Rambeau

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.020
Who grows up to become the Marvel hero Photon;
a.k.a. Pulsar

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.400
She also takes on the mantle of
Captain Marvel at one point

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.000
She's a major figure in the New Avengers

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.760
and perhaps a hero in the future Avengers films

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.040
If you look closely, one of the memories
features her stargazing with young Monica

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.000
as a shooting star zips across the night sky

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.040
And this brings up an interesting question
about the whole timeline of this movie

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:49.360
The main events are set in 1995

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.220
6 years after Carol left Earth in 1989

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:57.000
If Carol and Monica are seeing this shooting star,
say a year before she went missing

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.620
This could actually be Yondu's ship,
when he kidnapped a young Peter Quill

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:02.820
That was in 1988

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.340
And that is in Missouri, which isn't that far from Louisiana where the Rambeau home is

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:11.020
Carol calls Monica "Lieutenant Trouble",
which is also from the comics.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.980
It's a nickname given to Kit Renner

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.800
Who's a huge fan of Captain Marvel,
who like Monica in this movie

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.400
helps Carol recover her memories after amnesia

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.800
Now the target memory for Talos features
Dr. Wendy Lawson, the Earth alias of Mar-Vell

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.000
The project she works on is Pegasus,
which should sound familiar to you

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.220
Pegasus is the operation initiated by
the World Security Council

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.260
tasked with researching and weaponising the Tesseract

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.800
We actually saw the end of the Pegasus project
at the beginning of the Avengers movie

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:38.860
and Tony Stark mentioned it in Iron Man 2

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.380
"I need some stuff out of storage."

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.420
"Get me everything from projects
Pegasus, Exodus and Goliath."

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:46.400
Lawson appears to work for
an early incarnation of Pegasus

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.200
A joint operation between
the U.S. Air Force and NASA

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.760
Before it became a S.H.I.E.L.D. operation

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.400
Where, in the comics at least,
it was an acronym that stood for:

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.400
Potential Energy Group/Alternate Source/United States

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:58.200
Mouthful.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:02.000
Breaking free from her memory scrub,
Vers takes an escape pod to the planet's surface

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.800
Which turns out to be C-53,
a.k.a. Erf *derp face*

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.220
Now, the listed co-ordinates for Earth,
like all of the co-ordinates in this movie,

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.260
appear to be just random numbers and letters

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.800
But as we learned during our Easter egg hunts
in the Guardians movies

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.420
These co-ordinates might be code for something.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.840
All I could find was that E.R.D.E., Erde
is a German word for Earth

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.600
I dunno. Let me know if you find anything else

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.980
And now that she has returned to Erde, I'm just gonna call Vers "Carol"

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.000
Even though she doesn't yet remember
that her name is Carol

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.000
It's just because I think "Vers" sounds really stupid.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.600
CAROL crash lands in a Blockbuster Video

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:35.020
That's the first of many 90s references in
Captain Marvel

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:40.200
And this didn't rebrand its name to just "Blockbuster" until 1996, which is the year after this movie takes place

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.980
The movie titles visible around this Blockbuster include:

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.560
Last Action Hero

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:46.220
and a standy for True Lies

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:48.620
The directors for this movie,
Anna Boden and Ryan Fleck

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:51.620
said that 90s action movies like these
were big influences

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.720
Other influences included action movies like:

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.600
Total Recall

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.340
Independence Day

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.000
Men in Black

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Now, the movie title that she picks up is The Right Stuff

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:03.620
And that is actually a book and a film about air force pilots who train to be the first NASA astronauts

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:07.800
Similar to Carol's function as an air force pilot,
working on a joint mission with NASA

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.600
Outside Carol talks to this security guard in a parking-lot

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.180
She asks if he's in charge of security for this district

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:16.200
And says sort of, the movie theatre has its own guy

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:20.180
Now there's actually a great inside joke
that goes along with this, but before I get to that

00:09:20.180 --> 00:10:42.980
**Really long sponsor segment**

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.220
OK. Back to the security guard.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.380
This is actually a cameo by Barry Curtis

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:50.220
The director of on-set security for all of the Marvel films

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.980
This guy's responsible for
preventing leaks on Marvel's end

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:57.180
But as he says here, not responsible security in movie theatres themselves

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.580
By the way, this I think, is the Barry that
Mark Ruffalo was worried about pissing off

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:02.520
When he spoiled the ending of Infinity War

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.200
"Wait 'til you see this next one. Everybody dies."

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.000
"Dude!"

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.620
"Is Barry gonna be mad at me?"

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.480
Ah, I love that clip

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.000
Carol also mentions having a universal translator

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.400
Which is another nod to the
Guardians of the Galaxy movies

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:18.380
In which James Gunn established that all the alien races in this universe communicate via universal translators

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.380
As Carol uses parts from a RadioShack GameBoy to rig up a way to communicate with the Star Force

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.380
The wall behind her is covered in posters

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.980
Including some 90s "Rock the Vote" signs

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:32.400
And a poster for The Smashing Pumpkins 1995 album "Mellon Collie and the Infinite Sadness"

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:37.580
This could be a nod to Brie Larson's past role as
Envy Adams in Scott Pilgrim vs. The World

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.000
Which was adapted from the comics

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.020
in which her character debuted in an issue titled
"The Infinite Sadness"

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:45.000
Next arrives the other Marvel heroes
who get their origins in this movie:

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.180
S.H.I.E.L.D. agents Nick Fury and Phil Coulson

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.420
With Samuel L. Jackson and Clark Gregg

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:51.240
Digitally de-aged for their roles

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.420
Marvel's using the same process that they used on

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.980
Robert Downy Jr in Civil War

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.180
Michael Douglas, Michelle Pfeiffer and Laurence Fishburne in the Ant-Man movies

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.440
And Kurt Russell in Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 2

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.740
But here the VFX artists had to keep this up
for the whole movie

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:04.220
Not just limited parts of it

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.420
Jackson wore a wig and motion trackers on his face

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:09.440
But the guy was nearly 70 and they de-aged him so well

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.160
Ad for the more action heavy shots

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:14.400
The production actually swapped in
stunt actor Kiante Elam

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:17.400
who actually played
one of the extremist soldiers in Iron Man 3

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.200
This leads to a chase through
the street and metro lines of L.A.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:23.600
Which the directors based on the famous sequence in The French Connection

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:27.640
In which, Gene Hackman chased down a train car
from the street level below

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.220
The moment where Carol searches
through the train car for her target

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.360
Is a recreation of Hackman's search in that movie

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:34.780
Sitting in this car is, of course, Stan Lee

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.220
Making his traditional cameo

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:39.200
He's reading the script for the Kevin Smith movie "Mallrats"

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.360
Which he would make one of his first ever cameos in later in 1995

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.260
That's why he's actually credited as Stan Lee
in the credits of this movie

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.980
And he rehearses the line
*Stan impression* "Trust me true believer"

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.360
Which is actually what he tells Jason Lee in Mallrats

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.140
*Genuine Stan* "Trust me true believer"

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.660
Kevin Smith said that when he saw this while he was watching Captain Marvel it brought him to tears

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:01.480
Now, this fight between Carol and the old lady Skrull
is one of the highlights of the movie

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:06.080
Carol knows that she's a Skrull because, of course,
she passed by the real old lady earlier on the platform

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.180
And this fight is vicious!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:11.600
I love how you can see the woman's glasses
flying off her face when she gets punched

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.260
And the directors said they included a take where her dentures flew out when her head hit the pole

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:20.000
Actually, these flips and kicks are performed
on an actual moving train car by stunt performers

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.000
They're sisters, Renae and Heidi Moneymaker

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.980
The directors also just did a really good job

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:27.800
Pacing this fight between quick paced action and pauses for character reactions

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:30.820
Resulting in this intense growl from the Skrull
in the middle of the fight

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.000
And when the other passengers hold Carol back

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.800
Notice how the man behind her in a suit,
kinda looks different between takes

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.340
That's because in the earlier shot this was an extra

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.280
But in the close up
the guy who gets hit is a different actor

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.880
actually the movie's fight coordinator, Walter Garcia

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.640
He had to dress up like the original extra

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.640
when they reshot this scene
so they could add this little moment

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:53.300
When Carol gets off the train,
she passes this red-haired woman with glasses

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:57.600
This is a cameo by the Captain Marvel comic writer
I mentioned earlier, Kelly Sue DeConnick

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.300
The one responsible for
this whole incarnation of the character

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:03.400
As the Skrull who posed as Coulson
undergoes the autopsy

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.640
The S.H.I.E.L.D. medical officer
is played by actor Nelson Franklin

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.580
Who appeared in Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.
as agent Steve Wilson of the ATCU

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:14.120
An entity that deals with Inhumans,
though I don't think it's the same character here

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.200
Carol steals a motorcycle and gets
a new change of clothes from that mannequin

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:21.200
I actually think an earlier version of this scene
had her steal the guy's clothes too

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.300
In what might have been a reference to The Terminator

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:27.440
Underneath the jacket she wears
this Nine Inch Nails t-shirt. A nod to the 90s band

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.400
And the directors actually had to get special permission from Trent Reznor to feature this shirt

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.580
Carol meets Fury at the Poncho bar

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.840
And Poncho's is actually the name of a bar
mentioned in The Right Stuff

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:40.420
Near Edwards Air Force Base in California
where Air Force pilots would go hangout

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.640
The film's production put this Poncho's sign
over a different restaurant

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.000
The Zebra Lounge, which is also located in this area

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.780
Poncho's has a bunch of photos
of airplanes on the walls

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:52.840
And some of you asked in one of these is the Valkyrie, the Hydra bomber

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.940
That Captain America flew at the end of his movie

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:59.160
It's actually a Northrop YB-49 bomber
that was commissioned after World War II

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:03.720
And, yeah, it would be a little weird for this Air Force bar to have Hydra bombers on the wall

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.220
Carol and Fury get to know each other

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:09.020
And he says that before working for S.H.I.E.L.D.
he was a cold war era spy

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:10.080
Who worked in Belfast

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:10.820
Bukareszt

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:11.320
Belgrade

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:11.840
Budapest

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:12.840
He likes the Bs

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.940
And we actually learn another
B-named Fury outpost in Winter Soldier

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.580
When Cap' meets secretary Pierce

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:21.460
"That photo was taken 5 years after Nick and I met"

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.360
"When I was at state department in Bogotá"

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.000
Also it's interesting that Fury brought up Budapest

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.160
Because Marvel fans know, this could be a nod to another famous mission in Budapest

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:32.680
Referenced by Hawkeye and Black Widow in
The Avengers

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:34.620
"Just like Budapest all over again"

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.340
"You and I remember Budapest very differently"

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:38.940
Though, given the age difference here

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:43.980
Fury's Budapest mission was probably way earlier than whatever mission Clint and Natasha were a part of

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:47.420
Hopefully we'll see whole Budapest backstory
in Black Widow's upcoming solo film

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.940
Which is rumoured to take place
a few years before Iron Man in 2008

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:56.360
To prove he's not a Skrull, Fury tells Carol
that he can't eat toast if it's cut diagonally

00:15:56.360 --> 00:16:01.160
I love this detail, because if you look closely
at a specific shot in Age of Ultron

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.440
When Fury's with the Avengers on the Barton farm

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:07.600
He's cutting bread and some of you said
that it looked like it was being cut diagonally

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.940
But no! When he picks up the bread,
it's definitely cut down the middle

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:11.820
Not diagonally.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.400
Fury takes Carol to the Pegasus base in the desert

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:18.600
And he confirms that his full name is
Nicholas Joseph Fury, which is the case in the comics.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.840
Also, if you look closely at his badge,
it lists them as level 03

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:26.420
Now, that's pretty low for S.H.I.E.L.D. agents,
last time Fury was a part of S.H.I.E.L.D. he was level 10

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.000
So putting him at level 03 here

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.580
means that Fury wouldn't have
the same security clearance

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:34.660
to know everything what's going on with Pegasus
and what Dr. Lawson's research was all about

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:39.600
Now, it's not clear if this Pegasus base is the exact same one that we saw at the beginning of The Avengers

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:42.400
But, both are located in the Mojave Desert in California

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:47.140
But if you look at the terrain surrounding the whole
joint dark energy mission facility, it's a lot flatter

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.440
Whereas this is more rugged

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:52.820
Fury and Carol explore the records archives
and they run into Goose the cat

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.780
In the earlier memory, it was established that
he was a pet of Mar-Vell

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.400
And I guess he's still roaming this facility
6 years after she's gone

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.780
Now, in the comics, Carol Danvers' cat is named "Chewie"

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:03.600
Like the Wookie and brands of oatmeal bars

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.580
But here they named him Goose
after the character in Top Gun

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.120
In both instances, this cat is actually a Flerken

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.400
An alien species that resembles and Earth cat

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.780
They have tentacles in their mouths

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.500
They're able to swallow large quantities

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.640
In the comics, it's Rocket who outs the Flerken
and freaks out

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.820
Here, later on in this movie, it's Talos

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:23.220
Carol looks through Lawson's records and plans
for a light-speed engine

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.380
And realises from her notes that she was a Kree

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:28.200
And the movie actually teases a final reveal here

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.020
If you look at the old photograph of Carol

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.380
You can almost make out that her call sign,
on the side of her jet, says "Avenger"

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:34.200
Talos arrives

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.660
And the fact that he calls Fury "Nicholas"
tips off Fury that he's a shapeshifter

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.860
Leading to this whole fight

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:40.400
Now, there's an odd detail during this

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:43.960
In the scuffle, Fury defensively
unloads the clip from Talos' gun

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.780
But when he gets a hold of the gun later
he pulls the trigger on it

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:49.800
Now, I was thinking maybe Fury thought
one bullet could have been left in the chamber

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.660
But the directors acknowledge that Fury
just did this in the heat of the moment

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.200
Which is also probably why
Fury angrily throws the gun at him

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:58.180
Fury's saved when Carol
hits Talos with her photon blasts

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:00.020
Now listen closely to the sound design here

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:02.000
*sound with deep, rumbling thunder*

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.860
You can kinda hear a rumble of thunder

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:08.420
and overall it sounds a lot more organic
compared to the sound of Iron Man's repulsors

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.200
*high whining charge followed by a deep "pew"*

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:13.960
The directors wanted photon blasts
to sound more organic, more natural

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.600
Coming from within Carol's body

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:20.680
As opposed to the precise, mechanical,
defibrillator charge sound that Tony Stark's armour has

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.420
Carol and Fury escape in this jet

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:25.820
Which is a predecessor to the Quinjet
that S.H.I.E.L.D. will use later on

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:28.780
This is a fourth generation called the Quadjet

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.580
I look forward to the sixth generation model
The Sexjet

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:36.780
They arrive in Louisianna
where Carol reunites with Maria and Monica Rambeau

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.040
Talos surprises them
But if you look closely

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:43.200
The cup he's sipping from is the same design pattern
on the Big Kahuna Burger cup

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.000
That Jackson sips in Pulp Fiction

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.800
Talos says he stands before them as his true self

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:51.380
Whereas in the scene before with Ben Mendelsohn's actual appearance, that was an imposter

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:55.460
Now, notice how Mendelsohn in his Skrull form
speaks with his natural Australian accent

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.860
Whereas the human used his American accent

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.500
So now this is, in a way, his true form

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.740
Talos helps Carol understand the truth

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.180
With a black-box recording proving that Yon-Rogg

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:08.380
and the Kree Star Force were the ones
who shot down Carol and Mar-Vell

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:12.220
They pull this up from an old-school desktop CD-ROM that takes forever to load

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.200
Part of the movie's running joke of 90s computer tech

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:18.000
Like earlier we saw the AltaVista internet search engine

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.980
Carol finally recalls the origin of her powers

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.380
An explosion from Kree tech;
a light-speed engine built by Mar-Vell

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.560
Now, this is similar to Carol's origin in the comics

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.400
With the death of Mar-Vell
and an explosion leading to her powers

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:33.320
But the twist here is that the Skrull aren't the evil empire that the Kree propaganda suggested

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:37.620
They're actually refugees whom Mar-Vell was trying to help find a new home world

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:40.200
away from the Kree.
Using a light-speed engine

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:44.800
Carol was brainwashed by Yon-Rogg
using Kree blood transfusin and memory wipes

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:50.000
Now this is actually the same process that Nick Fury will later use to revive Coulson in Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.400
After his death in Avengers

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.200
Kree blood

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.000
Memory wipe

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.340
Perhaps Fury learned this process was possible from what ahppened with Carol Danvers

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:00.040
Carol works with Monica to help decide on
a new colour scheme for her suit

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.860
Now that she no longer aligns herself with the Kree

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:04.420
One of the options is red and yellow

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:06.040
Which Monica says "no" to

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:09.560
Perhaps because this is a colour scheme
of the other "Captain Marvel", Shazam

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.200
Another option is green and white

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.780
Which is actually the colour scheme of
the original Mar-Vell's Kree armour in the comics

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:18.160
And they head off to Mar-Vell's space lab
cloaked in orbit around Earth

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:22.380
Here they find the energy core that powered Mar-Vell's original light-speed machine

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.320
TA-DA!
The Tesseract

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.980
a.k.a. the Space Stone
One of the Infinity Stones

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:31.300
It, of course, has the power to open rifts in space and transport you anywhere in the universe

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.740
Its existence here is interesting

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:35.380
Because in the Marvel timeline

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.760
The last known appearance of the Tesseract was when Howard Stark recovered it from the ocean floor

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:40.700
At the end of Captain America

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.920
He presumably studied it for years thereafter

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:47.000
But now this movie is suggesting that it ended up in the hands of Dr. Lawson, a.k.a. Mar-Vell

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:50.000
I'll actually dig deeper into this whole Tesseract timeline in another video I'm working on

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:51.740
One interesting thing to note here

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:54.200
is that if the Tesseract powered the light-speed engine

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.440
that exploded and gave Carol her powers

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.940
You could argue that carol's powers
came from the Space Stone itself

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:04.800
In Infinity War, we learn that because Scarlet Witch's powers were derived from an Infinity Stone

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.820
She could destroy said Infinity Stone

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:10.700
So perhaps this means that Captain Marvel
could also destroy Stones

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.000
Potentially giving her a unique advantage in Endgame

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.000
This lab is littered with 90s era toys

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:18.020
because it contains hidden Skrull refugees and children

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:20.980
One of these toys is a Happy Days "Fonz" lunch box

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:22.600
That's what they used to store the Tesseract

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:24.600
But you can also see these troll dolls

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:27.400
Now, in the past I've speculated over
another possible link

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.340
between Guardians of the Galaxy and Captain Marvel

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:32.580
A throwaway line from Peter Quill about
a Kree girl he hooked up with

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:35.280
"Right here a Kree girl tried to rip out my thorax"

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.780
Now, we don't know where Captain Marvel's
heading off to in this ship at the end of the movie

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:40.560
Or where in the Galaxy she travelled

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.760
throughout the mid-90s and 2018
when she meets the Avengers in that post-credit scene

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.880
But we do know that Peter Quill hooked up with
some very aggressive Kree girl

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:51.480
or a human Earth girl who he thinks is Kree

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:57.560
And we know that Quill had at least one troll doll, because he used one to troll Yondu

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:01.780
So maybe a Captain Marvel sequel or a
Guardians of the Galaxy prequel

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:03.800
could show this whole fling

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.400
In this scene we can also see a Space Invaders pinball machine

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:09.580
but notice how the props department changed the art on the back of it

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:12.080
Perhaps because the original pinball machine
of Space Invaders

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.620
essentially stole the design of the Alien Xenomorph

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:18.200
The Kree arrive and for Carol back into stasis
with the Supreme Intelligence

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:21.200
But Carol breaks out by overpowering her inhibitor chip

00:22:21.200 --> 00:22:23.200
And she gives off this golden glow

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:24.420
She's super charged

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:26.580
In the comics, this is called "going binary"

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:30.660
Because Captain Marvel gets her power
from the energy of a white hole

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.580
The theoretical opposite of a black hole

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:35.420
In which infinite amounts of matter and energy
beam out of it

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:36.860
Carol blows back the other Kree

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:39.740
She tells Fury to "Take the Tesseract. Leave the lunch box."

00:22:39.740 --> 00:22:41.960
A nod to the Godfather quote
"Leave the gun. Take the cannoli."

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:44.500
Fury doesn't want to touch it, so Goose swallows it!

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:45.360
Awesome!

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:47.940
This actually echoes a joke by
Bruce banner in The Avengers

00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:50.000
"What does Fury want me to do? Swallow it?"

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.100
Uh-Oh, Ruffo spoiling future events again.
Somebody call Barry

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.620
As Carol goes full binary

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:56.240
Wipes out the Kree warships

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.420
Including the bombing raid by Ronan

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:00.040
Fury and Maria return to Earth

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:05.000
And as Fury takes Goose he tells the Flerken
"I'm trusting you not to eat me"

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:07.200
Now if you've been watching my videos
in recent months

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:10.580
You'll know that I gave a loud "HA!" to that line

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:11.980
Specifically the word "trust"

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:12.820
Yeah, roll the clip

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:15.920
"Last time I trusted someone, I lost an eye"

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:19.000
Fury trusted Goose who then
scratched his eye out

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:22.380
One of the few predictions I made for a movie
that, shockingly, came true

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:28.220
It also confirms why the wound over Fury's eye
was in the shape of a scratch from a cat paw

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:29.960
Fury shouts "Mother Flerken!"

00:23:29.960 --> 00:23:32.640
because it's Sam Jackson
He's gotta work in a "Mother *beep*" in there

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:36.200
It's also a nod to the way "Flerken"
is used as a profanity in the comics

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:38.800
Like when Carol says "no one steals my Flerken cat!"

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:40.840
After Carol destroys all of Ronan's bombs

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:45.300
She stares him down from space
and he promises to return for her

00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:48.380
So that explains why we don't see him become
the whole rogue extremist

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:50.460
that he is in Guardians yet in this movie

00:23:50.460 --> 00:23:54.340
Presumably there's more story to tell with him
in a future Captain Marvel film

00:23:54.340 --> 00:23:55.060
Back on Earth

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:58.800
Maria and Fury escape the pursuing Kree ship
through a canyon

00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:02.720
It's very evocative of the Captain Hiller
dog fight in Independence Day

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:06.060
And when Carol confronts Yon-Rogg in the desert,
she drags him back to his ship

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:10.120
Similar to how Hiller "welcome to Earth" 's the alien
and drags him across the desert

00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:12.160
As they wind down back at the Rambeau house

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:14.320
Fury tells Carol to go by a new name

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.580
And although the words "Captain Marvel"
is never said out loud in this movie

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:22.320
Fury does give her the inspiration by singing
the Marvelettes "Please Mr. Postman"

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:23.860
Now you may know this song from the Vine meme

00:24:23.920 --> 00:24:29.220
*Memeing it up*

00:24:29.220 --> 00:24:33.380
This would be the second time in recent memory a Marvel origin movie referenced a Vine meme

00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:36.320
After Shuri's "What are those?" line in Black Panther

00:24:36.400 --> 00:24:38.760
*Reference meme*

00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:40.900
Also Carol returns Fury's pager

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:43.960
Which she confiscated earlier after he used it to call her into Talos

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:46.320
She spruced it up to boost its signal across galaxies

00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:49.760
Setting up the post-credit scene in Infinity War
and in this movie

00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:52.620
Check out my other video for more details that
you might have missed in the post-credit scene

00:24:52.620 --> 00:24:55.380
And that brings us to the final scene in Nick Fury's office

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:59.900
Coulson brings Fury various options for a prosthetic eye to replace the one that Goose scratched out

00:24:59.960 --> 00:25:02.060
But Fury prefers his eye patch

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:07.460
Most likely because he likes this whole bad ass myth narrative that he lost it during a Kree interrogation

00:25:07.460 --> 00:25:08.900
But there could be another reason

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:12.680
Like Fury now knows that Skrull shapeshifters exist in this universe

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:14.620
The ones that he met were relatively friendly

00:25:14.620 --> 00:25:17.920
But there may be others out there
with more nefarious goals

00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:21.100
This scratched eye is one unique marker on Nick Fury

00:25:21.100 --> 00:25:22.800
If he keeps it covered with the patch

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:27.480
There's no way any Skrull could know, from sight alone, what his eye wound look like

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:30.180
So if S.H.I.E.L.D. were compromised in the future

00:25:30.180 --> 00:25:35.060
And a Skrull tried to copy Nick Fury, all the real Nick Fury would have to do is lift his eye patch

00:25:35.060 --> 00:25:37.220
As a way to prove that he is the real one

00:25:37.220 --> 00:25:40.440
The final detail dovetails this movie
directly into The Avengers saga

00:25:40.440 --> 00:25:43.300
Fury's writing up his proposal for
"The Protector Initiative"

00:25:43.300 --> 00:25:47.440
His and Coulson's idea to find other heroes
like Captain Marvel out there to protect Earth

00:25:47.440 --> 00:25:50.920
But upon seeing her call sign in her old photo "Avenger"

00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:52.520
He re-names this initiative

00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:57.460
If you listen closely to the music, you can hear
Alan Silvestri's iconic march of The Avengers' theme

00:25:57.460 --> 00:25:59.980
But to be honest, we never do see what he writes

00:25:59.980 --> 00:26:00.660
Could have been anything

00:26:00.660 --> 00:26:02.020
The Flerken Initiative

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:02.780
Who knows

00:26:02.780 --> 00:26:06.980
But I'm curious to know from you guys
Which spinoff story would you like to see next?

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:10.180
Captain Marvel vs the whole Kree and
the Supreme Intelligence and Hala?

00:26:10.180 --> 00:26:13.520
Or maybe a prequel with
Carol and the Guardians of the Galaxy?

00:26:13.560 --> 00:26:17.300
Or a new Skrull secret invasion storyline?

00:26:17.320 --> 00:26:20.420
With some other, more evil, terror cell

00:26:20.420 --> 00:26:21.720
And if secret invasion

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:26.600
Which Marvel hero do you want to be established as a Skrull in disguise all this time?

00:26:26.600 --> 00:26:29.400
And why is it Hawkeye? Let the guy live in peace.

